      "id": 1,
      "text": "Weston was named by Larkin Adamson after his hometown of Weston, Missouri.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.westontexas.com/page/about_us",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Adamson opened Weston's first store in 1850 and became its first postmaster on January 16, 1854.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.westontexas.com/page/about_us",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Settlers arrived in the early 1840s, attracted by the fertile Blackland Prairies and water from Honey Creek and the East Fork Trinity River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.westontexas.com/page/about_us",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Weston sits at the crossroads of Farm Roads 543 and 455, eleven miles northwest of McKinney.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
